      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While Vitamin C is an antioxidant, relying on high-dose supplements for kidney stone prevention is not a proven treatment. High doses of Vitamin C can actually increase oxalate levels in some individuals, potentially worsening calcium oxalate stones. It's crucial to discuss any major dietary or supplement changes with your nephrologist to create a safe and effective management plan tailored to your specific stone risk.",
      "source": "target",
